A Route arms with one end.
The router would wire an event to whatever its channel last named, or the other way round;
a Route is armed only with both its ends.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: route is armed without both its ends
Witness: fuzz route-arms-with-both-ends

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -830,7 +830,7 @@ static int op_route(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, const
         if (arg[1] > 1) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
-        if (arg[1] == 1 && (r->ends[ROUTE_EVENT].type == CAP_NONE || r->ends[ROUTE_TASK].type == CAP_NONE)) {
+        if (arg[1] == 1 && r->ends[ROUTE_EVENT].type == CAP_NONE && r->ends[ROUTE_TASK].type == CAP_NONE) {
             return KERR_STATE;
         }
         route_arm(r, arg[1] == 1);
